<title>SWEDEN: Nordbanken posts 10 pct fall in Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>Nordbanken posts 10 pct fall in Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bank Nordbanken on Tuesday posted these earnings for the first quarter of the year, ending on March 31.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>Operating profit</p>
<p> after loan losses			 1,402 vs 1,561</p>
<p> Loan losses				   110 vs   280</p>
<p> Net interest income		     2,493 vs 2,599</p>
<p> Net commission				553 vs 505</p>
<p> Financial transactions, net   CHARGE  128 vs 245 CREDIT</p>
<p> Other income				  168 vs  66</p>
<p> Total income				3,086 vs 3,415</p>
<p> Operating costs			   1,574 vs 1,574</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	     1,512 vs 1,841</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	    5.35 vs 6.14</p>
<p>Adjusted equity/shr (crowns)  excluding dividend			95.40 vs 101.06</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts in a Reuter poll expected a profit of 1.70 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-017</p>
</text>
